WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:04.740
"Indiana Jones and the Dial of Destiny"&nbsp;
was supposed to be a graceful swan song&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.740 --> 00:00:09.480
for the beloved adventure hero, but it&nbsp;
instead seems to have been…a poor choice.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.660 --> 00:00:12.360
Here's why it's not clicking&nbsp;
with audiences like expected.

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:17.460
Although the box office numbers are disappointing&nbsp;
– according to Variety, "Dial of Destiny" pulled&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.460 --> 00:00:21.180
in an $82 million domestic gross&nbsp;
over its first five days of release,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.180 --> 00:00:26.760
with a production budget of nearly $300 million –&nbsp;
the movie is actually doing pretty well in terms&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:31.920
of its critical reception. It has settled at a 68&nbsp;
percent rating on the Rotten Tomatoes Tomatometer,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:36.360
giving it "Fresh" status, and it has an&nbsp;
overwhelmingly positive audience score of 88&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.360 --> 00:00:41.480
percent. But Indy's final adventure started things&nbsp;
off on the wrong foot with its early reviews.

00:00:42.480 --> 00:00:43.480
"Shhh."

00:00:43.480 --> 00:00:49.800
In May 2023, star Harrison Ford premiered&nbsp;
the movie at the 76th Annual Cannes Film&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.800 --> 00:00:54.240
Festival. The critical reactions from that&nbsp;
showing were mixed-to-negative. Critics&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.240 --> 00:00:57.660
including Owen Gleiberman of Variety&nbsp;
and Manohla Dargis of The New York&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.660 --> 00:01:01.020
Times wrote about their disappointment&nbsp;
regarding various elements of the film,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.020 --> 00:01:04.500
such as its generic blockbuster&nbsp;
movie feel and uneven plot.

00:01:04.500 --> 00:01:08.340
For several weeks, the Cannes reaction&nbsp;
dominated the conversation surrounding&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.340 --> 00:01:12.180
the movie's quality. That early negative&nbsp;
buzz certainly didn't do the movie any&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.180 --> 00:01:15.480
favors in its pre-release marketing,&nbsp;
even if it did ultimately turn out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.480 --> 00:01:18.720
to be far more warmly received by&nbsp;
those that bothered to go see it.

00:01:18.720 --> 00:01:22.740
"Dial of Destiny" isn't the first time that&nbsp;
Hollywood has attempted to resurrect this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.740 --> 00:01:28.200
storied franchise. In 2008, nearly two decades&nbsp;
after "The Last Crusade," came "Indiana Jones and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.200 --> 00:01:32.580
the Kingdom of the Crystal Skull." The fourth film&nbsp;
in the series attempted to move the story forward,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.580 --> 00:01:37.080
placing an older and wiser version of&nbsp;
Indy in the midst of a 1950s conspiracy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.080 --> 00:01:40.680
narrative full of Cold War intrigue.&nbsp;
Fans weren't too happy with the result,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.680 --> 00:01:45.480
decrying the film's formulaic approach to&nbsp;
recreating the spectacle of the original movies.

00:01:45.480 --> 00:01:49.020
They also didn't love questionable&nbsp;
new elements like the character of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.020 --> 00:01:53.460
plucky youngster Mutt Williams, played by Shia&nbsp;
LaBeouf, who notably doesn't return for "Dial&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.460 --> 00:01:57.420
of Destiny." For some viewers, "Kingdom&nbsp;
of the Crystal Skull" was proof that the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.420 --> 00:02:00.900
"Indiana Jones" franchise would be better&nbsp;
off left to rest in the glory days of old.

00:02:02.040 --> 00:02:04.560
"Knowledge was their treasure."

00:02:06.360 --> 00:02:09.180
It's unlikely, then, that those fans&nbsp;
will be convinced to watch a second&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.180 --> 00:02:12.780
revival in "Dial of Destiny," no matter&nbsp;
how much of an improvement it may be.

00:02:13.380 --> 00:02:17.160
"Dial of Destiny" is far from the only&nbsp;
movie of its kind to have underperformed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.160 --> 00:02:20.280
this year. There are other examples&nbsp;
from even the same month of release,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.280 --> 00:02:26.340
June 2023. DC's massive superhero blockbuster&nbsp;
"The Flash" similarly bombed at the box office,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.340 --> 00:02:30.420
and Pixar's "Elemental" also vastly&nbsp;
underperformed. All of these movies&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.420 --> 00:02:35.172
are major productions attached to big studios&nbsp;
and intended to appeal to general audiences.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.172 --> 00:02:39.744
It seems that "Dial of Destiny" is facing some&nbsp;
issues that are endemic to the greater industry.

00:02:39.744 --> 00:02:43.320
While there's no definitive answer to the&nbsp;
problem plaguing the blockbuster movie scene&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.320 --> 00:02:47.520
at the moment, there are a few factors to&nbsp;
consider. Theaters have somewhat managed to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:47.520 --> 00:02:51.660
recover from their struggles from the COVID-19&nbsp;
pandemic, but there are still ripple effects.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.660 --> 00:02:55.980
Would-be moviegoers seem to be more selective&nbsp;
regarding which movies can draw them back&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.980 --> 00:03:00.600
into darkened theaters full of other people.&nbsp;
There's also the matter of franchise fatigue.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.600 --> 00:03:04.800
The general landscape of the film industry is&nbsp;
currently filled with all manner of sequels,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:04.800 --> 00:03:09.600
nostalgic revivals, reboots, and action-packed&nbsp;
superhero flicks, and it's possible that the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.600 --> 00:03:14.460
luster of a new "Indiana Jones" movie, among other&nbsp;
franchise fare, has been considerably dulled.

00:03:14.460 --> 00:03:17.640
The fact of the matter is that not&nbsp;
everyone who wants to see "Dial of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.640 --> 00:03:21.960
Destiny" is going to do so in theaters. Yes,&nbsp;
the film debuted exclusively in cinemas,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.960 --> 00:03:25.080
but it's only a matter of time until&nbsp;
it becomes available to stream at home,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:25.080 --> 00:03:28.260
and interested viewers may be content&nbsp;
to wait until then to watch it.

00:03:28.260 --> 00:03:32.340
There's currently no set date for when "Dial&nbsp;
of Destiny" will become available to watch at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.340 --> 00:03:36.120
home through Disney+ and other services, but&nbsp;
there probably won't be too long of a wait&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:36.120 --> 00:03:41.160
if precedent holds. Most recent Disney movies,&nbsp;
including as "Ant-Man and the Wasp: Quantumania"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.160 --> 00:03:45.900
and "Black Panther: Wakanda Forever," arrived on&nbsp;
Disney+ and other digital storefronts somewhere&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:45.900 --> 00:03:50.760
around 90 days after their theatrical release.&nbsp;
That means that audiences likely only have to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:50.760 --> 00:03:55.164
wait a matter of months until "Dial of Destiny" is&nbsp;
available to watch in the comfort of their homes.

